From 56386f66b771bbecba8abe36cb50d6389a22ae4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Qwen (Arena agent)" <agent@arena.local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 06:47:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] feat(seo): mount the buyer Q&A band, emit FAQPage, ship
 brand rasters

Follows the user's answers to the three confirmation questions raised at the
end of Revision 3.

Q&A / AEO FAQ layer (user chose "mount the section and emit the markup"):
- the home page now renders <QaSection /> immediately after <PricingPlans />
  (the band's own copy references the #pricing grid above it), restoring the
  section qa-data.ts documents and qa-section.tsx always implemented but no
  page imported
- <JsonLd data={faqJsonLd(HOME_QA)} /> is emitted for exactly the entries that
  section renders, so the markup matches visible content as Google requires.
  The two are coupled on purpose: removing the component must remove the markup
- page.test.tsx's designed-heading sequence gains the new band in position;
  the file's one remaining failure (contributor count) is pre-existing

Brand rasters (user chose "generate both"):
- public/brand/logo-512.png: the repository's own logo.svg monogram cropped to
  its measured artwork box and padded square, transparent - rendered with
  sharp, not AI-imagined, so the graph shows the real mark
- public/brand/og-default.png: 1200x630 share card on the paper token with the
  brand blue/navy bands, the monogram, and the wordmark + tagline set in
  Liberation Sans (the only font available to the offline renderer - the one
  typographic compromise design may redo)
- BRAND_ASSETS in lib/seo.ts is the single place both live: Organization.logo
  now points at the raster (schema.org ignores SVG) and the root layout reads
  the card into openGraph.images and twitter.images, so twitter's declared
  summary_large_image finally has an image to render

Tests: seo.test.ts now pins logo to the raster path and keeps sameAs omitted.
38 seo/surface tests pass; web suite 776 passed with the same 10 pre-existing
failures verified against clean HEAD earlier; tsc and eslint clean.
